terraform-provider-railway-next

This project includes an independent Go implementation of Railway environment
graph and change-set behavior informed by the public source of Railway's
MIT-licensed railway-ts-sdk:

  https://github.com/railwayapp/railway-ts-sdk
  Version studied: v3.6.0
  Commit studied: dd3a11ea140059149079a91045efc454b21cdbc4

No source code from the TypeScript SDK is imported or executed by the provider.
The SDK's MIT license remains available in its upstream repository.

Contributors
------------

  Jon Bogaty — https://github.com/jbdevprimary

    Four fixes found by running the provider against a live Railway account:
    resource ids lost during updates (`UseStateForUnknown` on all nine
    resources), `environmentApplyChangeSet` never waiting for completion, a nil
    private-network endpoint crashing `terraform import`, and a service source
    racing the change set when attached through `serviceConnect`.

    Two additions: the `railway_deployment_trigger` resource, without which a
    service never deploys, and private network addresses exposed as attributes.
